# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Frontend (Vite) — these ship in the browser bundle.
# ONLY public-safe values belong here. The Supabase anon /
# publishable key is safe client-side ONLY when Row Level
# Security is enabled on every table. Never put the service
# role key, or any private API key, in a VITE_ variable.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
VITE_SUPABASE_URL="https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co"
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="your-supabase-anon-publishable-key"
VITE_SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID="your-project-ref"

# Non-prefixed duplicates used by some tooling (still public-safe values only)
SUPABASE_URL="https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co"
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="your-supabase-anon-publishable-key"

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Server-side secrets — DO NOT put these in this frontend .env
# and never prefix them with VITE_. They are configured as
# backend/edge-function secrets, not in client code:
#   GEMINI_API_KEY              (Google Gemini)
#   OPENAI_API_KEY              (OpenAI)
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY           (Anthropic)
#   DIALAGRAM_API_KEY           (Dialagram)
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY   (full DB access — server only, never client)
#   SUPABASE_DB_URL             (Postgres connection string — server only)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
